{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Deletion executed (2026-08-12) — the encoded DELETE ruling, carried out\n\nResumed now that the blocker cleared: e369 is CLOSED, so parent epic 5796 is claimable and\nthe parent-first cascade no longer fast-fails. The prior session's attestation could not be\nreused (it verified as `foreign_key` — signed by a different environment principal), so\n`review-plan` was re-run in this environment: **PASS, signed**. Claim then succeeded.\n\n**Re-proved the port is dead in the fresh worktree before touching it**, both ways per\nAGENTS.md. Serena `find_referencing_symbols` on `SupportsAbsenceProbe` and on\n`SupportsAbsenceProbe/probe_remote` returned EMPTY (with `find_symbol` resolving the same\nsymbols, so the file is genuinely indexed and the empty result is real). A repo-wide string\ngrep for the whole surface hit ONLY the port itself, its own tests, and prose. The two\nknown false positives were re-confirmed as unrelated: `_commands/_init_probe.py::probe_remote_branch`\nprobes a git remote BRANCH, and the OUTBOUND probe leaf is live and untouched.\n\n**What landed** — 28 files, 73 insertions / 1033 deletions. Deleted outright:\n`inbound_probe.py`, `adapters/jira/probe.py`, `adapters/jira_family/probe.py`, and the\nthree probe-only test modules. Removed: `SupportsAbsenceProbe` and all three\n`probe_remote` implementations, plus `classify_probe_response` from the `jira_family`\nexports. Both stale docstrings claiming a by-path load of `inbound_probe.py` are corrected.\n\n**Two deviations from the plan text, both recorded rather than silently absorbed:**\n\n1. **ADR 0035 has been renumbered to 0083** (`docs/adr/0083-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md`)\n   since the plan was written. Same file, same edit — the module-list entry for\n   `inbound_probe.py` is dropped.\n2. **The config-read gate caught the orphan the plan deferred, and it is a hard CI blocker.**\n   `scripts/check_config_reads.py` fails when a schema field has no attribute-read site;\n   deleting the classifier left `JiraConfig.resolved_statuses` with none. (DC's\n   `reconciler.resolved_statuses` still reads into the transport, so only the Cloud field\n   fires.) I did NOT remove the key — that is the user-visible surface change this ticket\n   explicitly defers. Instead I used the gate's own first-class affordance for exactly this\n   case: a `# read-via:` marker whose pointer names a rebar ticket, which the gate REPORTS\n   rather than errors on and whose justification expires when that ticket closes. It is\n   parked against the follow-up, 549c-032f-6cb0-4258. The gate's companion invariant test\n   (`test_the_real_schema_has_no_marker_parked_against_a_ticket`) is amended to pin EXACTLY\n   one parked marker naming that ticket — deliberately exact rather than a bare non-empty\n   check, so a second unrelated field cannot be parked unnoticed. This adds\n   `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` and `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` to\n   the blast radius; `file_impact` is updated to the actual 28 files.\n\n**AC5 amendment on e369 is done**: the probe classifier is dropped from its\n\"one shared implementation imported by both backends\" clause, recorded as a comment on e369\nwith the reasoning that this is a scope reduction (the shared unit ceased to exist along\nwith the capability it served), not a per-adapter fork.\n\n**Follow-up filed and linked**: restful-chaseable-macaw (549c-032f-6cb0-4258),\n`discovered_from` this ticket, carrying the deprecate-vs-remove decision for the orphaned\n`resolved_statuses` keys and their DC transport plumbing.\n\nGates: `make lint` and `make typecheck` green; full unit suite re-running against the final\ntree. Next: push to Gerrit for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786519714928954001,"uuid":"0ad2469e-5efd-4bb9-a606-1039abe482f6"}